title Why text has to be measured first
align center
col
  w 100%
  maxw 640
  pad 20
  gap 14
  fnt 24
  fg 235 240 255
  txt Why text has to be measured first
  fnt 12
  fg 120 140 170
  txt A page about the page engine
  fnt 15
  fg 190 205 230
  txt A layout engine has to know how tall a paragraph is before it can place whatever comes after it. The height depends on how many lines the paragraph needs, and that depends on the width it is given. So the order is always the same: decide the width, break the text into lines, count the lines, and only then move on.
  txt Tiny broke text into lines while painting. By then every box already had its place, so a paragraph that needed three lines still had the height of one and ran over the element below it. Pane breaks the lines during layout, which is why this paragraph pushes the next one down however narrow the window gets.
  fnt 18
  fg 235 240 255
  txt What changes with the width
  fnt 15
  fg 190 205 230
  lst
    txt On a phone the column is the width of the screen, less the padding.
    txt On a desktop the column stops growing at 640 pixels and sits in the middle.
    txt A word that is wider than the line, such as a long address, is broken between characters: https://example.org/a/very/long/path/that/would/otherwise/run/off/the/side/of/a/small/screen
  end
  txt Rows work the same way. Each child of a row gets a share of the width, the text inside it is broken to fit, and the row becomes as tall as its tallest child.
  row
    gap 12
    col
      bg 14 24 42
      pad 10
      txt Left column. It has more to say than the right one, so it needs more lines and sets the height of the row.
    end
    col
      bg 14 24 42
      pad 10
      txt Right column.
    end
  end
  fnt 18
  fg 235 240 255
  txt Scrolling
  fnt 15
  fg 190 205 230
  txt The page is taller than the window, so it scrolls: wheel, drag on a touch screen, or the arrow, Page and Space keys. Only what is on screen is painted.
  txt A scroll area inside the page scrolls on its own until it reaches its end, and then the page takes over.
  scl 120
    bg 10 18 32
    pad 10
    gap 6
    txt Line one of a small scroll area.
    txt Line two.
    txt Line three.
    txt Line four.
    txt Line five.
    txt Line six.
    txt Line seven, the last.
  end
  div
  lnk Back to the start page home
end
